    {{!-- jet skiing--}}

    <div class="game_name">
        <div class="game_title">
            <h3>jet skiing</h3>
            <p>
                <b>Jet skiing</b> is a thrilling water sport that involves riding a personal watercraft (PWC), commonly
                known
                as a Jet Ski, on open water. Here's some information about jet skiing:

                <br> <b> Watercraft:</b> Jet skis are small, motorized watercraft powered by jet propulsion. They are
                designed to be
                ridden by one or two passengers.

                <br> <b> Controls:</b> Riders stand or sit on the jet ski and use handlebars to control direction and
                throttle to
                control speed. Jet skis are known for their agility and maneuverability on the water.

                <br> <b>Safety Gear:</b> It's crucial to wear safety gear when jet skiing, including a life jacket,
                wetsuit, and, in
                some cases, goggles or a helmet.

                <b>Types of Jet Skiing:</b>

                <br> <b> Recreational Riding:</b> Many people enjoy jet skiing for leisure, riding on lakes, rivers, or
                oceans for
                fun and excitement.
                <br> <b> Racing:</b> Jet ski racing is a popular competitive sport with various categories and events
                held worldwide.
                Stunt Riding: Some experienced riders perform tricks and stunts on jet skis, including jumps and flips.
                <br> <b> Touring: </b>Guided jet ski tours are available in many coastal and waterfront destinations,
                allowing riders
                to explore scenic areas.
                Safety Measures: Jet skiers are expected to follow safety regulations and guidelines to ensure safe
                riding. This includes respecting speed limits, maintaining a safe distance from other watercraft, and
                avoiding reckless behavior.
                <br> <b> Age and Licensing:</b> The age requirements and licensing regulations for jet skiing vary by
                location. In
                some places, operators must have a boating license or specific jet ski endorsement.
                <br><b> Environmental Responsibility:</b> Riders are encouraged to be environmentally conscious and
                avoid areas with
                sensitive ecosystems, as the powerful watercraft can disturb wildlife and damage aquatic environments.

                <br> <b> Maintenance:</b> Proper maintenance of the jet ski is essential to ensure its safe operation.
                Regular
                inspections, engine checks, and maintenance of safety equipment are necessary.

                <br> <b> Popularity: </b>Jet skiing is a popular activity at coastal resorts, lakes, and tourist
                destinations,
                drawing enthusiasts of all ages. It offers an exciting way to experience the water and explore new
                areas.

                <br> <b> Safety Awareness:</b> Riders should be aware of potential hazards, such as currents, boat
                traffic, and
                weather conditions, and take precautions accordingly.
                <br> <b> Jet Ski Brands:</b> Several companies manufacture personal watercraft, with some well-known
                brands being
                Kawasaki (originator of the term "Jet Ski"), Sea-Doo (by BRP), and Yamaha. These brands offer a range of
                models suitable for various types of riders and purposes.

                <br> Jet skiing combines speed and agility with a close connection to the water, making it an enjoyable
                and
                thrilling watersport for those seeking an adrenaline rush or a fun day out on the water. It's important
                to prioritize safety and adhere to local regulations to ensure a safe and enjoyable jet skiing
                experience.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="game_imgs">

            <img class="img1" src="images/jet_1png.jpg" alt="">

